# Specification maintenance (Guardian Angel)

After you finish a **substantive** change to this repository (behavior, HTTP APIs, env vars, Firebase layout, Docker/runtime, data models, or operator-facing UI), **reconcile documentation** before ending the turn:

1. Open **`GUARDIAN_ANGEL_SPEC.md`** and update **Version**, **Last updated** (use the user’s authoritative session date when known), and any sections that no longer match the code or deployment story.
2. If the change touches how components integrate (Firebase, FastAPI, Uvicorn, Docker, networking), update **`documentation/TECH_STACK.md`** in the same pass when appropriate.
3. **Skip** spec churn for typo-only edits, comment-only changes, or formatting-only diffs.

Treat the spec as the **contract** for Guardian Angel: if the implementation diverges, either fix the code or update the spec—do not leave both contradictory.
